1. Definitions

  1.1. "Engine" means the VoxelCore software, including its source 
       code, binary files, and documentation, unless otherwise 
       explicitly stated.

  1.2. "Unmodified Version" means an exact copy of an official 
       release of the Engine, distributed by the Copyright Holder or 
       authorized parties, without any changes.

  1.3. "Modified Version" means any version of the Engine obtained by 
       altering its source code or binary files, including adding, 
       removing, or changing any files that are part of the Engine.

  1.4. "Pack" means software that interacts with the Engine solely 
       through its public API, scripting interfaces, network protocols, 
       or data formats, and does not include the Engine's own code. A 
       Pack is an independent work and is not considered a derivative 
       of the Engine.

  1.5. "Game" means a collection of packs and/or other resources 
       (data, scripts, content) intended for use together with the 
       Engine. A Game may include an Unmodified Version or a Modified 
       Version of the Engine; however, if a Modified Version is 
       included, the Game is subject to the restrictions applicable to 
       Modified Versions (Section 3.2).

  1.6. "Commercial Use" means any use aimed at obtaining direct or 
       indirect financial benefit, including but not limited to: sale, 
       rental, provision of access, inclusion in commercial products, 
       provision of services, or use as part of paid services.

